<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Ammon</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 BCE – 582 BCE (approx.) · capital Rabbah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ammon, an Iron Age kingdom of the Jordanian plateau around Rabbah, modern Amman, whose name lives on in Jordan's capital.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ammonites formed a kingdom in the 10th century BCE or earlier, on the plateau around the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabbok">Jabbok</a> river, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amman">Rabbah</a>, the citadel of modern Amman. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Bible</a> portrays King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahash-of-ammon">Nahash</a> as an enemy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saul">Saul</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ammonite kings ruled a farming and herding land guarded by watchtowers, under the national god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milcom">Milkom</a>. Inscriptions such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amman-citadel-inscription">Amman Citadel inscription</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-siran-bottle">Tell Siran bottle</a>, which names King Amminadab, show a language close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a>. Ammon prospered as a loyal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baalis">Baalis</a> plotted against Babylonian rule in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Judah</a>. A Babylonian campaign in 582 BCE ended Ammon's independence, and the land became a province. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amman">Rabbah</a> was refounded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ammon.jpg" alt="Ammon" width="320" height="382"><figcaption>Image: FinnWikiNo; derivative work by Richardprins... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdoms_around_Israel_830_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 BCE – 582 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rabbah</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nahash, Amminadab, Baalis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ammonite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ammonite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Ammon, Ammonites</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-791&amp;focus=ammon" aria-label="Ammon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5622 1054 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ammon lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0M6140 1251h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5942 1310h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5942 1310h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Jordan. <a href="/atlas?year=-791&amp;focus=ammon">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

